{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>The precepts of</b> — from the root of פקדון (deposit). They are those found in the power of the soul in every person when he reaches obligation in commandments, and HaShem deposited them in the heart. And he mentioned ישרים alongside them, for all who are discerning grow wise through them in the straight path, wherein there is no stumbling." "<b>rejoicing the heart</b> — for through them the wise man attains the rank of eternal joy. And corresponding to the sun he mentioned ישרים, because the sun's course is upon the bands of the wheel of the zodiac, and that is the straight path. And the precepts further surpass, for the sun at times deviates from the plane of the ecliptic, and 'rejoicing of the heart' corresponds to the sun, for thus it is only 'in the day you shall rejoice' and not at night, whereas the precepts rejoice always. And 'the commandments of YHWH' — these are positive commandments, and he called them מצות because for most of them it is not written why they were commanded. And he said of them ברה, for so they are to the pure of heart; therefore 'enlightening the eyes' — like a man who was in darkness. And corresponding to the sun he said ברה, for there is in it no semblance of dimness within it, as with the moon. And the superiority of the commandment: clouds hide the light of the sun by day, but not so the commandment — and 'enlightening the eyes,' for it is the light of the world by day and also by night, for the light of the moon indicates through complete proofs."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:53.494844912Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}